id: pm-github-dependabot-merge
title: Reusable Dependabot merge workflow with complete commit provenance
description: "Replace copied auto-merge logic with a reusable workflow that revokes stale requests and only arms verified Dependabot-only PRs. Companion: pm-cli-website-wis6."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[6]: changelog-unreleased,ci,dependabot,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#221",security,workflows
created_at: "2026-11-05T00:19:21.862Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T08:21:47.911Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Only pull_request events with Dependabot author and actor plus a complete trusted commit list and allowed metadata can arm squash auto-merge.; Foreign authors or committers, metadata failures, API errors, stale heads and unsupported events cannot arm; existing requests are revoked with sanitized notices and summary.; Execute regression cases for opens, rebases, foreign author, foreign committer, major update, over 100 commits and API failures; verify real fleet commit provenance.; Migrate the own caller, document release SHA pinning and extra groups, regenerate changelog and run package gates."
comments[30]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-05T00:19:41.701Z",codex-agent,"No duplicate open item found. Plan: revoke before metadata, load the standalone TypeScript policy only from the reusable workflow commit, check every paginated commit with verified web-flow exception, then arm using an expected-head lease. Real API read of pm-context#211 confirms Dependabot author with verified web-flow committer and a foreign-author/foreign-committer addition. No PR source is checked out or executed. GitHub auto-merge is asynchronous: callers must retain protected-branch checks; revocation on synchronize cannot provide an atomic server-side invariant for future pushes."
  "2026-11-05T00:33:47.214Z",codex-agent,"Implemented trusted-policy loading, pre-tooling revocation, verified web-flow handling, complete paginated commit/count/head proofs, metadata allowlist and head-bound squash requests. Focused suite: 66 passed. Behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy: removing only the foreign-commit filter made 12 of 61 tests fail; restored suite passed. Read-only production-policy execution against real pm-context#211 refused its foreign addition; all mutation calls were receipts only. Older local gh lacks --slurp, so production uses --paginate with JSON-line output. Documented write-token requirements, first-release pin placeholders and the asynchronous GitHub auto-merge limitation. Full npm tests now running serially before coverage."
  "2026-11-05T00:39:54.549Z",codex-agent,"The linked pm test run passed all 67 focused cases in plain temporary directories. Strengthened provenance to require valid GitHub verification for both accepted committer accounts, because account attribution can be forged via Git email fields. The 101-commit case now keeps the first page independent and puts the foreign committer only on page two. Pre-tooling revocation and policy-load failures are executable workflow tests. A policy-load API failure produces a successful refusal with summary/notice; inability to revoke is an explicit operational failure. Typecheck, test typecheck, ESLint, docstrings, zero duplication, zero production audit vulnerabilities and the existing object-store privacy audit passed. Changelog regenerated after fetching tags; check passed."
  "2026-11-05T00:41:20.832Z",codex-agent,"Additional review: --match-head-commit is an expected-head check, not a durable server-side lease; protected-branch requirements remain necessary for a literal future-push guarantee. Proposed diff scan through the current source runTrackerGate passed: 8 files, 644 added lines, zero findings, zero allowlist entries. The installed pm github gate command instead returned one absolute-host-path finding without an offset for the same diff; current source scanning finds none. This installed-command/source divergence is a PM extension UX gap to report, not changed here."
  "2026-11-05T00:45:42.353Z",codex-agent,"Final regression corpus: 68 focused tests passed through the pinned pm test runner. Repeated the behavioral revert against the final policy in a disposable copy: removing only the provenance filter caused 13 failures and 55 passes; the package worktree was never mutated. Added a real-API edge case: closed or merged PRs can retain historical auto_merge metadata, so only active requests are revoked. Current typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass. The full npm suite is still progressing through existing closeout integration cases; coverage and complete release gates remain pending."
  "2026-11-05T00:47:36.608Z",codex-agent,"PR opened: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/221 at aaffdb6da1a6a5cea010f125aa562fb5cb6fbd72. Published title, feature-item link, plain-text companion reference and public-safe body were read back and verified. Code commits: dd46efa and aaffdb6. The full npm suite is still running; PR body explicitly marks complete release and coverage gates pending. No source changes are planned unless a gate finds a defect."
  "2026-11-05T00:52:55.096Z",codex-agent,"Read-only Actions workflow API verification found dependabot-auto-merge.yml is disabled_manually. No workflow state was changed. Created follow-up pm-github-dependabot-activation for reviewed activation, token provisioning, protected-branch requirements and controlled live acceptance. This delivery migrates the source caller; it does not establish that repository automation is enabled. CodeQL passed on aaffdb6; the CI matrix is queued or starting."
  "2026-11-05T01:06:36.970Z",codex-agent,"The focused suite now passes 69 tests, adding the exact fresh-open state with auto_merge=null alongside the existing armed-request revocation case. Test typecheck, ESLint and docstring gate pass after this addition. The first existing closeout workflow integration scenario passed; current long subprocesses are fixture package installs and workflow execution. Source policy behavior remains unchanged from aaffdb6; only helper documentation and the new acceptance case were added."
  "2026-11-05T01:11:46.208Z",codex-agent,"Fixture timing isolated repeated npm registry/cache checks as a major local bottleneck: the same existing numeric-pagination workflow case passed in 299.94 seconds normally and 67.47 seconds total with NPM_CONFIG_PREFER_OFFLINE=true and the public npm configuration. Interrupted the first full npm run with exit 130 after verifying and stopping only its own process group; it is not counted as passing. Restarted the entire suite with cache preference, NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null, isolated Git config, low priority and at most two workers. Versions, fixtures, assertions, coverage scope and thresholds are unchanged; missing packages still use the registry. The focused suite remains 69 passed."
  "2026-11-05T01:19:54.725Z",codex-agent,"CI on aaffdb6 found one related integration failure: the publication-attestation scanner treated TypeScript template literals in the quoted workflow heredoc as unresolved shell execution. The run reported 1712 tests, 1711 passes and 1 failure, with all four source coverage percentages at 100; this is not a passing gate. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41943832975/job/126970983903 . Replaced only the generated launcher template literals with string concatenation. The attestation gate now passes, and the combined production-policy plus attestation suite passes 77 tests. No scanner policy, thresholds or merge decisions were changed. Full local npm tests continue using the public npm configuration and cache preference."
  "2026-11-05T01:26:13.405Z",codex-agent,"Corrected code is pushed at e12d12ec1f117ef95f53f92048bc23d6012997b0. CodeQL passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41947808408 . Current CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41947808424 . Verified the superseded run belonged to PR 221 and branch feat/reusable-dependabot-merge before cancelling its remaining jobs to free capacity for the corrected head; the original failure receipt is retained and no cancellation is counted as approval. A real raw-contents API fetch at e12d12e is byte-identical to scripts/dependabot-merge.ts (SHA-256 d9a8c70f2aeffe832f840a1402701b64d9731d7d49ea85892e90ca359015e799). Final 69-case provenance revert proof gives 13 failures and 56 passes; the pinned linked test runner passes all 69 afterward."
  "2026-11-05T01:43:50.312Z",codex-agent,"Review found and fixed a custom-token event loop in the caller: auto_merge_enabled events can belong to the automation credential owner, so subscribing to them would immediately revoke a valid bot-only request under the required actor guard. Removed that event from the own caller and README snippet; synchronize remains subscribed. Added a two-event regression that executes the production policy: token-generated arm events preserve the request, then a foreign synchronize revokes it. Reintroducing only the old event subscription in a disposable copy makes that one behavioral test fail; the unchanged package worktree passes all 70 policy/workflow tests. Combined policy and publication-attestation tests pass 78 cases. Test typecheck, lint and publication-attestation gate pass. No predicate, permissions, thresholds or branch configuration changed."
  "2026-11-05T02:05:48.106Z",codex-agent,"Native Bun found two default-adapter fixture failures: Bun command lookup used its startup environment when child_process options omitted env. A unique local-command probe reproduced the difference without network access: implicit lookup failed under Bun while an explicit environment resolved the fixture on Node and Bun. The earlier dynamic-PATH default-gh probe escaped its intended stub and was rejected against the synthetic target; no arm or squash operation was requested. The adapter now snapshots the current environment explicitly, and default-adapter coverage runs in child processes with fixture PATH present at startup. Added a unique-command regression; reverting only the environment option makes that one Bun test fail without any real gh fallback. Fixed source passes 71 native Bun tests and 79 combined Node policy/attestation tests. Pinned pm linked test execution also passes. Test typecheck, lint and docstrings pass."
  "2026-11-05T02:16:17.850Z",codex-agent,"Current source head b1e8285b1ff8896d9c81de3ca92a9b93ed2e6eec has passing CodeQL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41952923845 . CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41952923878 was manually cancelled under the repository owner account before any job steps started; check-run annotations confirm the cancellation. This is missing validation evidence, not approval. No rerun was requested for that manually cancelled run. Local full npm tests continue through the existing end-to-end closeout decision matrix; the complete npm and Bun release gates will run serially afterward. Native local runtime receipts are Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5."
  "2026-11-05T02:36:47.382Z",codex-agent,"Caller ownership review retained the original PR-author-only filter in the thin caller and documented it in the migration snippet. This preserves other PR automation while still invoking the reusable workflow when a foreign actor pushes to a Dependabot-authored PR. The reusable policy itself retains all author/actor/provenance checks and revocation behavior whenever invoked. Workflow policy tests require the caller author guard and forbid caller actor guards; the two-event foreign synchronize regression still passes. Current receipts: 71 native Bun passes and 79 combined Node policy/attestation passes. Final-policy real API refresh at b1e8285 is byte-identical to the repository script (SHA-256 8063b11c33820d662187bcd5a6741ede744a447be16484d2dc97be4630023356), refuses the real pm-context#211 foreign addition and performs zero mutation calls. Remaining release gates will use the already installed Node 26.13.0 through nvm, matching the CI runtime line; the active npm test run remains Node 24.19.0."
  "2026-11-05T03:08:03.967Z",codex-agent,"At the 30-minute CI cutoff for source head 773283e4eae83e1b7d130afc92997e1007cdd628, CodeQL passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41956452617 . CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41956452612 still has test (22), test (26), bun-release (22) and bun-release (26) in progress. These are pending, not approval; CI polling for this head stops here. Independent local required gates continue. The low-priority full npm suite has passed the closeout matrix, sync publication boundaries and the 500-sequence SDK state-model regression, with no failures reported so far."
  "2026-11-05T03:31:24.213Z",codex-agent,"Completed the low-priority Node 24.19.0 npm test run: 1714 passed, zero failed, cancelled or skipped; elapsed 8140.26 seconds. It began before the final three new regression cases, so the fresh final-source release gates will execute the updated corpus. Early shell state projections now reject incomplete open-PR data instead of treating a missing auto_merge field as unarmed; malformed input forces a revocation attempt. Real jq tests cover malformed data and closed historical metadata. Reverting only the projection makes the malformed-state behavioral test fail. Launcher and bootstrap processes now explicitly use non-git temporary working directories, rather than merely storing their files there. Current final focused receipts: 73 native Bun passes, 81 combined Node policy/attestation passes, and successful pinned pm test execution. Test typecheck, lint and publication-attestation checks pass."
  "2026-11-05T03:51:57.488Z",codex-agent,"The first Node 26 release-gate attempt passed prechecks and entered coverage, then was interrupted with exit 130 to isolate inherited agent-session and credential context from synthetic fixtures. It is not counted as passing. Installed SDK source confirms automatic Codex session-provenance capture; CI has no such inherited session context. Restarted the unchanged complete release command in a CI-like child environment with agent/provider credentials and context excluded, public npm configuration, cache preference, empty GitHub credential configuration and isolated Git config. Parent agent configuration and project data remain untouched. All tests, source inventory, thresholds and the two-worker bound are unchanged; no other local suite runs alongside coverage."
  "2026-11-05T03:56:25.085Z",codex-agent,"Read-only follow-up confirmed the previous candidate CI run completed successfully: Node 22, Node 26, Bun release on Node 22 and Bun release on Node 26 all passed. This receipt applies to commit 773283e only; the latest stricter malformed-state receipt checks are being verified separately. CodeQL and Semgrep passed for 850e964; its four CI jobs remain in progress. Local final release coverage is running alone after all prechecks passed."
  "2026-11-05T03:56:44.272Z",codex-agent,"Strict tracker health reports settings, storage, locks, integrity and append-only history all healthy, but exits 1 on extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew: the pinned host is 2026.10.25 and the package is 2026.11.4. This existing version relationship is unchanged; dependency bumps are owned by Dependabot and are outside this task. The warning is retained as a validation limitation rather than weakening health or altering the SDK pin."
  "2026-11-05T03:59:45.842Z",codex-agent,"Clarification of the strict-health warning: installed SDK source shows extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew compares the CLI host version with the CLI copy resolved by a loaded extension, not the extension package version itself. The warning names 2026.10.25 and 2026.11.4. The tracked lockfile and local pinned host both remain 2026.10.25. Disabling extensions for the separate integrity receipt produces all ten checks healthy with zero warnings; normal extension-enabled health remains a disclosed warning."
  "2026-11-05T04:01:40.883Z",codex-agent,"Exact source-head 850e964 CI Bun release gate passed on Node 26: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41962134164/job/127030715983 . The complete bun run release:check command passed with 1717 tests, zero failures, zero production audit vulnerabilities and 100 percent lines, statements, branches and functions across the unchanged full source inventory. Local native Bun 1.3.5 focused suite separately passed 73 tests. Other current CI jobs and the local npm release coverage are still running; no incomplete run is counted as approval."
  "2026-11-05T04:02:50.796Z",codex-agent,"The 30-minute CI observation cutoff for source head 850e964 has been reached. Run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/41962134164 has Bun release on Node 26 successful; npm on Node 22, npm on Node 26 and Bun release on Node 22 were still in progress at the last snapshot. CodeQL and Semgrep succeeded; skipped or neutral bot reviews are not approval. Further CI polling for this head stops at this cutoff. Independent local release coverage continues serially."
  "2026-11-05T04:20:01.108Z",codex-agent,"Final source-head gate receipts for 850e964: the complete npm run release:check step succeeded on Node 26 at 04:05:55 UTC and Node 22 at 04:12:18 UTC; both Bun release jobs succeeded as well. All four commands used the unchanged full release gate, including exact full-inventory coverage. The Node 26 Bun log confirms 1717 passing tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips and 30 modules at 100/100/100/100. The npm CI jobs still run their later native Bun phase, so whole-job completion is distinct from the completed npm gate. After verifying these receipts, the duplicate local release attempt was interrupted and is not passing evidence. The earlier low-priority npm test run passed 1714 tests; the final 73-case policy corpus passed under Node and native Bun, with the combined attestation suite at 81. No duplicate local Bun full gate is needed after actual exact-source CI execution of that command. No local full test process is intentionally left running."
  "2026-11-05T04:20:53.947Z",codex-agent,"Implementation handoff is ready for review: all seven required policy scenarios are covered in the 73-case production-policy/workflow suite; combined publication-attestation coverage is 81 tests, and the commit-provenance behavioral revert produces 13 failures. Exact-source npm and Bun release gates passed on both supported Node lines in CI with unchanged thresholds. Runtime activation remains separately blocked in pm-github-dependabot-activation: the workflow is disabled and write-token/server-protection acceptance is outside this PR. GitHub asynchronous auto-merge cannot provide an atomic future-head lease; the documented branch-protection requirement remains material. The future release-pin placeholder is intentional because this feature is not in a published release. Installed-command/source diff-gate divergence and extension CLI version skew are disclosed validation-tool limitations. No merges, releases, secret changes or thread replies were performed. Releasing only the codex-agent claim; both items remain open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-05T08:11:45.790Z",codex-agent,"Review round on 2652cc9: fetched all three unresolved threads with complete comments and latest review body; merged origin/main first (650797d). Valid fixes: bounded gh calls and revocation retries in TypeScript and both shell paths; README owner claim; --auto fixture assertion; local-only main policy override. Also evaluating the unverified web-flow attribution concern. Plan: behavioral regressions and isolated reverts, full npm and Bun release gates serially under nice, append-only tracker evidence and explicit-path commit. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-11-05T08:16:42.288Z",codex-agent,"Review body unverified provenance claim: no supported forgery demonstrated. GitHub documents createCommitOnBranch (including web commit behavior) as authenticated-user authorship with no custom author/committer; bot verification requires bot/App authentication without custom identity fields. Rebase-and-merge cannot obtain a generic GitHub system signature. Existing corpus rejects foreign committers even when verified and unsigned web-flow/bot attribution; verified Dependabot/web-flow is intentional for real fleet commits. Sources: https://docs.github.com/en/graphql/reference/commits#createcommitonbranch and https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/managing-commit-signature-verification/about-commit-signature-verification . Retaining this documented exception; generic signature validity alone is insufficient, and the policy also enforces author/committer and event identities. GitHub asynchronous merge and compromised credentials remain the previously documented server-protection boundary."
  "2026-11-05T08:18:23.452Z",codex-agent,"Implemented all four actionable review findings. githubCli bounds each process with SIGKILL after 60 seconds and at most three attempts; both bootstrap shell paths bound every read, policy download and disable call identically, discard failed output, and report an explicit potentially-still-armed failure on exhausted revocation. Workflow job limit is 30 minutes. job.workflow_ref plus the caller pull-request merge ref limits trusted-main selection, preserving remote SHA-pinned self-calls. Focused Node and native Bun each pass 85 tests; pinned pm linked runner passed 85. Shell fixtures execute real shortened timeout calls against TERM-resistant finite stalls and retry successes. No thresholds changed; dist is generated and untracked."
  "2026-11-05T08:19:31.969Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable non-git copy with unchanged new tests: restoring githubCli from 2652cc9 causes 3 failures/0 passes; removing only timeout+SIGKILL causes 1 failure/2 passes; reverting both shell paths to unbounded gh causes 8 failures/11 passes; restoring repository-only main override causes remote-self 1 failure; removing only production --auto causes 3 success-path failures; restoring README owner claim causes 1 failure. Fully restored copy passes 85/85. Reviewed whole PR diff for these classes: every gh call in both shell blocks is now wrapped, every policy call goes through bounded githubCli, and remote external and self-pinned loaders retain their SHA. Follow-up budget review increased the job cap from the initial 30 to 60 minutes and bounds setup and metadata individually to 5 minutes; this leaves room for worst-case revocation retries instead of cutting off the final fallback."
  "2026-11-05T08:21:47.910Z",codex-agent,"Final focused validation: pinned pm linked Node and native Bun runners each pass 85 tests, zero failures/skips. Focused c8 measures scripts/dependabot-merge.ts at exact 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Test typecheck, ESLint, docstrings (271 declarations), zero-threshold duplication and regenerated changelog check pass. Starting the unchanged full npm then Bun release gates serially with nice, a credential-free child context and isolated Git config; complete release and coverage results are pending. Commit identity range contains only the required approved bot email."
